meta {
  name: Apply Stocktake
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/restaurants/{{restaurant_id}}/inventory/stocktake
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
      "notes": "Monthly count",
      "counts": [
          {
              "inventory_item_id": "{{item_id}}",
              "counted_qty": 42,
              "notes": "Two bags torn",
              "waste": {
                  "quantity": 2,
                  "reason": "damaged"
              }
          }
      ]
  }
}

docs {
  Owner/manager. Each counted line is adjusted to counted_qty.

  waste (optional, per line): part of the shortfall that was thrown away.
  - quantity > 0, no more than what the count found missing (422 on counts.N.waste.quantity otherwise)
  - reason: expired | spoiled | damaged | other
  It is logged in the waste register (waste_entries.stocktake_id) first; only the rest of the shortfall becomes the adjust movement.

  Each variance row returns waste_qty, waste_reason and unexplained_variance (variance + waste_qty).
}
